  ('99c4d3ad-ed27-4225-a383-7cae2270f5c0', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$A writer, John, was struggling with writer's block. He felt like his creativity had 'struck out', but he refused to 'cower'. He continued to write, even if it was just a few words a day, believing that his 'determination and commitment' would eventually lead to his 'home run' – a completed novel. He knew that his journey was 'destined' to be challenging but ultimately rewarding.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('0c6db337-ae1d-4db4-8bd6-da798183ede8', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$A student, Emily, was preparing for a debate competition. She felt intimidated by her opponents, but she adopted the 'I will' spirit from the poem. She prepared diligently, knowing that her 'proactive approach' and 'strong resolve' were essential. She aimed to deliver her arguments with 'courage', believing that her 'effort' would be recognized, regardless of the debate's outcome.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('4a889df6-b23a-470c-9722-8a86f8047494', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Some think bravery is living without fear, But that is not true. Bravery is living despite the fear, And doing what needs to be done Even though you are scared. Some can stand on the sidelines of life, And be content with what could have been, but never was. That is not me. I will not look back at the end of my life Thinking of what could have been. I vow to live my dreams no matter what; I will stand up and be counted. Even when I’m one of the few or standing all by myself. I will proudly state before God and all who see This is who I am and what I want to be. I will stand proudly in the batter’s box On the baseball field of my dreams And I will not cower at the thought of being hit.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 30, NULL),
  ('8b2efcca-08c1-4f2f-9d1f-3ae2cf387ab1', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Or feel ashamed if | should strike out. That will not only echo in my heart and If | do not achieve all that | desire mind, It will not be for lack of courage or effort But in all those who were destined to witness | will go down swinging as if my life My Success. depended on it. P And maybe in that moment, But if all | want is meant to be, Courage will be found Then, | will hit a home run. Searching for the strength to be brave.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('c51016ab-27e1-45cb-a403-8f4a5ffe97d0', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem emphasizes determination and resilience. For instance, the phrase 'I will' is an example of Anaphora, which is the repetition of words or phrases at the beginning of the lines. This repetition signifies determination and commitment, expressing a strong resolve and a proactive approach towards achieving goals. Furthermore, the poem introduces several vocabulary terms: 'blissful' (in a state of peaceful happiness or satisfaction), 'cower' (to crouch down in fear), and 'destined' (certain to meet a particular goal by fate).$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('561aa94a-37aa-4925-ad99-ef800b734ea5', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poet's unwavering spirit is evident throughout the lines. They declare, 'It will not be for lack of courage or effort,' highlighting the importance of sustained endeavor. The idea of 'going down swinging as if my life depended on it' underscores an intense commitment. Even the possibility of failure, 'striking out,' is met with a refusal to feel 'ashamed.' This resolute stance is further supported by the understanding that success, if 'meant to be,' will eventually lead to a 'home run,' but not without the active 'searching for the strength to be brave'.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('2f14543c-1be2-4808-9510-bb2f69f9dab7', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's vocabulary enriches its themes. For example, 'despite' means without being affected by, which is crucial for maintaining resolve in the face of obstacles. The concept of an 'echo,' a sound reflected off a surface and heard again, is used metaphorically to describe the internal impact of actions or feelings. To 'witness,' meaning to observe, connects to the idea of others recognizing one's success. The poem, along with its analytical notes, is presented in an English-8 context, suggesting its use for understanding literary devices and thematic interpretation.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('d1268639-c270-47c9-a8ae-04fedcc75306', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem presents a powerful assertion: 'The repetition of the phrase ‘I will’ in the poem signifies determination and commitment. Reason (R): The phrase ‘I will’ expresses a strong resolve and a proactive approach towards achieving goals.' This highlights the deliberate choice of language to convey the poet's unwavering spirit. The poem's message is not just about individual triumph but also about the journey, the effort, and the internal fortitude required to pursue one's desires, even when the outcome is uncertain.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('de180001-39e9-4891-b188-4feff6dfe4d7', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's opening lines immediately establish a tone of defiance against potential failure: 'Or feel ashamed if I should strike out.' This sets the stage for a narrative of resilience. The subsequent lines, 'It will not be for lack of courage or effort,' reinforce the poet's self-awareness and commitment. The idea of 'going down swinging' further solidifies this image of relentless pursuit, suggesting that the process of striving is as important as the outcome itself. The poem encourages readers to embrace challenges with a proactive and determined spirit.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('46b825fd-6fa3-433c-aa00-c4a245354b6a', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's central theme revolves around the poet's unwavering resolve. The declaration, 'I will go down swinging as if my life depended on it,' encapsulates this commitment to relentless effort. This spirit is further supported by the refusal to 'cower' or feel 'ashamed' in the face of potential failure. The poem suggests that true strength lies in the continuous 'searching for the strength to be brave,' rather than in an inherent absence of fear. This active pursuit of courage is key to achieving one's 'home run'.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('62a23886-895f-498a-841c-3c002138aeb3', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem introduces the concept of 'destiny' with lines like 'destined to witness My Success' and 'if all I want is meant to be.' This suggests an interplay between fate and personal endeavor. While the poet commits to maximum 'effort' and 'courage,' there is an acknowledgment that some outcomes might be predetermined. However, this belief in destiny does not diminish the poet's 'proactive approach' but rather frames the potential 'home run' as a fulfillment of a larger plan.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('e8fee416-90a7-4dd4-9078-fa936de2487b', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's emotional depth is conveyed through its exploration of 'shame' and the internal 'echo' of unfulfilled desires. The poet explicitly states that if desires are not achieved, it will 'not be for lack of courage or effort,' implying that the internal 'echo' would be the absence of this lack, rather than the lack itself. This highlights a profound self-awareness and a commitment to internal integrity. The poem suggests that true regret stems from insufficient effort, not from the outcome itself.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('3190ef52-5d00-465b-a059-6769f0182be6', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem, presented in an English-8 context and supported by 'NEP Guidelines,' serves as an excellent tool for understanding literary analysis. The identification of 'Anaphora' with the example 'I will' demonstrates how specific literary devices contribute to the poem's overall impact. The vocabulary definitions, such as 'blissful' and 'despite,' further enhance comprehension, allowing students to grasp the nuances of the poet's message about determination and facing challenges 'without being affected by' adversity.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('c19906dc-800c-45fb-a9f3-790c7bfe39fc', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poet's journey is depicted as one of intense personal struggle and aspiration. The metaphor of 'striking out' represents potential failure, which the poet vows to face 'without shame.' This is contrasted with the ultimate goal of 'hitting a home run,' symbolizing success. The poem emphasizes that this journey requires a continuous 'searching for the strength to be brave,' indicating that courage is not a static trait but an ongoing quest. The poet's commitment is to 'go down swinging,' signifying a refusal to yield.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('737b6687-74d4-4d97-a8a2-fa90fef717cc', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's message extends beyond individual triumph, suggesting that 'My Success' will be witnessed by 'all those who were destined to witness.' This introduces a communal aspect to achievement, implying that personal victories can inspire or impact others. The poet's 'strong resolve' and 'proactive approach' are not just for self-gratification but also for fulfilling a larger, perhaps fated, role. This perspective adds depth to the theme of determination, connecting individual effort to a broader human experience.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('997b6a5a-c999-499c-b1c5-fe5e091dcf00', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem highlights the internal battle against fear and self-doubt. The act of 'cowering' is explicitly defined as 'to crouch down in fear,' which the poet implicitly rejects through their resolute stance. Instead, the poet embraces the challenge of 'searching for the strength to be brave,' indicating an active process of overcoming fear. This internal struggle is crucial to the poet's journey, as it is in these moments that true 'courage' is forged, leading towards the possibility of a 'home run'.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('4e6d893c-ca2d-4bba-b8cc-a4647e0aefbb', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's language is direct and impactful, reinforcing its message of unwavering commitment. The repetition of 'I will' acts as a powerful affirmation of the poet's 'determination and commitment.' This anaphora creates a rhythm that underscores the relentless nature of the poet's 'effort.' The phrase 'as if my life depended on it' further intensifies this commitment, conveying a sense of urgency and ultimate importance to the pursuit of desires. This linguistic choice ensures that the poet's resolve is unmistakable.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('ddb9f110-f43e-49e4-8a85-e7c414a1efb5', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem presents a nuanced view of success and failure. While 'striking out' is a possibility, the poet's refusal to feel 'ashamed' redefines failure not as an end, but as a moment to be faced with dignity. The ultimate 'home run' is conditional on 'if all I want is meant to be,' suggesting that while effort is paramount, there is also an element of fate. This balance between human agency and destiny provides a realistic yet hopeful perspective on achieving one's 'desires.'$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('f697a320-5743-45e3-a37b-1dc5a361c977', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's themes resonate with the importance of internal fortitude. The 'echo' in the 'heart and mind' is not of external judgment but of personal integrity regarding 'courage or effort.' This internal accountability drives the poet's 'proactive approach' and 'strong resolve.' The poem suggests that true satisfaction, or 'blissful' happiness, comes from knowing one has given their absolute best, 'despite' external outcomes. This emphasis on inner strength is a core message.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('7940c4ed-d2a8-40d8-ac28-f3041f9a9197', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem serves as an inspirational text, particularly for young learners. Its focus on 'determination' and 'perseverance' aligns with educational goals of fostering resilience. The clear definitions of vocabulary like 'witness' (to observe) and 'destined' (certain by fate) enhance linguistic comprehension. By encouraging students to explore the 'theme of determination' using tools like 'Cordova Smart Class Software,' the poem integrates literary study with practical application, preparing students to face their own challenges with a 'proactive approach.'$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('151afad4-82b0-434f-ba9a-375b0bb569f6', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poet's commitment to 'go down swinging' is a powerful declaration of intent. It signifies a refusal to surrender, even when success is uncertain. This attitude is reinforced by the assertion that failure will 'not be for lack of courage or effort,' placing the responsibility squarely on the individual's dedication. The poem thus champions the process of striving, emphasizing that the value lies in the fight itself, rather than solely in the 'home run' outcome. This perspective encourages a relentless pursuit of 'desires.'$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('81491c6b-69af-4919-b574-e7811a51afde', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's structure, with its use of anaphora, creates a sense of building momentum and conviction. The repeated 'I will' acts as a rhythmic affirmation, driving the narrative forward and solidifying the poet's 'strong resolve.' This deliberate repetition ensures that the central message of 'determination and commitment' is deeply ingrained. The poem's progression from acknowledging potential 'shame' to embracing the 'strength to be brave' showcases a journey of internal growth and unwavering spirit.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('a3becdab-944b-4df5-8ddb-58aaee20fe43', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem offers a profound insight into the nature of true 'success.' It's not merely about achieving a 'home run' but also about the integrity of the 'effort' and the presence of 'courage.' The idea that 'Courage will be found Searching for the strength to be brave' suggests that success is intertwined with an ongoing process of self-discovery and fortitude. The 'blissful' state of satisfaction comes from this internal journey, making the external outcome a culmination rather than the sole measure of achievement.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('9d18ddd4-18bb-4778-ac99-cc0421d11faa', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's message is timeless, transcending specific contexts. Its emphasis on 'determination' and a 'proactive approach' to life's challenges is universally applicable. The metaphors of 'striking out' and 'home run' are easily understood, conveying complex ideas about failure and triumph in relatable terms. The poem encourages readers to cultivate an inner resilience, ensuring that even if 'all I want is meant to be,' their personal 'effort' and 'courage' are the driving forces behind their journey.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('d2af6d54-f441-4c22-8248-9ed45472f6c4', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem implicitly critiques the notion of passive acceptance or giving up prematurely. By stating 'It will not be for lack of courage or effort' if desires are not met, the poet places a high value on sustained struggle. The commitment to 'go down swinging' is a direct counterpoint to 'cowering' in fear. This active stance against surrender reinforces the poem's core message that true failure lies not in the outcome, but in the absence of genuine, persistent endeavor.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('51e68e8e-89bf-4a7c-9630-587fcfcd436e', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's use of the word 'despite' ('without being affected by') is crucial for understanding the poet's resilience. It highlights the ability to maintain focus and effort regardless of external pressures or setbacks. This mental fortitude allows the poet to pursue 'all that I desire' with an unwavering spirit. The poem suggests that true strength comes from an internal locus of control, where external circumstances do not dictate one's commitment or 'courage.'$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('24014bfa-4e43-455e-8da0-e9b86634c3c4', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's exploration of 'destiny' adds a layer of philosophical depth. The idea that some individuals are 'destined to witness My Success' suggests a predetermined audience or impact. This doesn't negate the poet's 'effort' but rather frames it within a larger, perhaps cosmic, plan. The phrase 'if all I want is meant to be' further reinforces this, implying that while the poet strives, the ultimate outcome may align with a grander design. This blend of free will and fate is a compelling aspect of the poem.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('aaf766eb-0a53-48ac-92ff-06e8becf85c3', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's focus on 'courage' is not about the absence of fear, but the active pursuit of strength in its presence. 'Courage will be found Searching for the strength to be brave' implies an ongoing, internal quest. This contrasts sharply with 'cowering' (to crouch down in fear), which represents a surrender to fear. The poet's journey is thus one of continuous self-empowerment, where bravery is cultivated through conscious effort and resolve, ultimately leading to the possibility of a 'home run'.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('7f1fedc0-f193-44a5-89c0-b1bd981f5df8', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's message about 'determination and commitment' is reinforced by the 'proactive approach' expressed through the repeated 'I will.' This is not a passive hope but an active declaration of intent. The poet's willingness to 'go down swinging as if my life depended on it' underscores the intensity of this commitment. This proactive stance ensures that even if 'all I want is meant to be,' the poet has played an active, indispensable role in shaping their own 'Success.'$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('2cb3af53-a8a2-4695-be48-f1fc6ac2210d', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's emotional impact is heightened by the concept of the 'echo' in the 'heart and mind.' This internal resonance of actions and feelings serves as a powerful motivator. The poet's vow not to feel 'ashamed' if they 'strike out' suggests a deep understanding of self-worth that is independent of external outcomes. This internal 'echo' of integrity and effort is more significant than any external judgment, driving the poet towards their 'desires' with unwavering resolve.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('46696f75-9554-4c3b-b67a-2dffc2c096bd', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's use of the term 'blissful' (in a state of peaceful happiness or satisfaction) suggests that true contentment comes from the journey and the effort, not just the destination. Even in the face of potential 'striking out,' the poet's commitment to 'go down swinging' implies a 'blissful' acceptance of having given their best. This redefines success to include the satisfaction derived from persistent 'effort' and 'courage,' regardless of the final 'home run' outcome.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('4954b228-0c7b-4b21-8e4a-7df12ed9d96e', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's message is particularly relevant in an educational context, as indicated by its inclusion in 'English-8' and reference to 'NEP Guidelines.' It encourages students to adopt a 'proactive approach' to learning and challenges, emphasizing 'determination and commitment.' The exploration of literary devices like 'Anaphora' and vocabulary terms like 'destined' and 'witness' enhances critical thinking and linguistic skills. The poem serves as a powerful tool for fostering resilience and a growth mindset among learners.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL),
  ('40671f77-a121-48b9-9c8d-b599adb117e8', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '995323c5-784e-45a4-84e7-517dcd6d1b16', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem's central conflict is the internal struggle against giving up. The poet's resolve to 'go down swinging' and not to feel 'ashamed' if they 'strike out' is a testament to this struggle. The idea that 'Courage will be found Searching for the strength to be brave' highlights the active nature of overcoming this conflict. This internal battle, rather than external circumstances, is the true test of the poet's 'determination and commitment,' ultimately defining their path to 'Success.'$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-326Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 5, NULL);
